From ace38751d8ba081b54273390ec2214f330c930f9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 17:04:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] volume_manager: Fix missing <vector> include

VolumeManager.h uses std::vector in its VolumeWatcher interface and
elsewhere but never included <vector> directly. Without it,
std::vector<std::string> fails to parse in VolumeWatcher::handleEvent's
pure virtual declaration, and the resulting error-recovery type
mismatch then makes VolumeClient::handleEvent (volclient.h) look like
it hides an overload with a different signature -- a cascading
-Werror=overloaded-virtual that goes away once the real parse error is
fixed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: Ib5d52a62a3a752698c6a45e4de26e3d5220c0e52
---
 volume_manager/include/volume_manager/VolumeManager.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/volume_manager/include/volume_manager/VolumeManager.h b/volume_manager/include/volume_manager/VolumeManager.h
index c2cb8dde..74d653b3 100644
--- a/volume_manager/include/volume_manager/VolumeManager.h
+++ b/volume_manager/include/volume_manager/VolumeManager.h
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include <list>
 #include <mutex>
 #include <string>
+#include <vector>
 
 struct selabel_handle;
 class NetlinkManager;
